If that is all that is needed, Robin has the authority as jatna to=20
implement much of his proposal, in particular that which pertains to the=20
period before "the job gets done".

When he can certify that "the job is done", the members will=20
(presumably) approve a new baseline, and it becomes more appropriate to=20
debate what happens then (preferably in Lojban, a sentiment that Robin=20
hearkens to himself).

If the membership thinks that the 5 year freeze promised in the baseline=20
statement is too long, or simply wrong, they can and will amend it very=20
simply as part of the new baseline declaration that will supplant the=20
existing statement.  The current statement itself indicates that there=20
will be decisions made at that time about the post-baseline role of the=20
"rump-byfy"

